			}
			for _, a := range absErrs {
				// absolute errors are like "/tmp/.../main.go:2:8: msg" (with absolute). Need to format as "<pos>: <msg>"? But they already are "pos: msg". For our parts, we need "pos: msg" without extra prefix? Actually for absErrs, each is already "pos: msg" (like "/tmp/...: msg"). When joining with space inside "[...]", they appear as "/tmp/...: msg". Good. But need to handle that relErr part already has "-: " prefix, while abs parts have no prefix? In observed message, after relErr, abs parts appear as "/tmp/...: ..." without extra prefix, just space-separated. Good.
				// However, our absErrs from parser/types are already "pos: msg" (absolute). Good. Just append as is? But need to ensure they are space-separated, not newline-separated. Our parseErrs/typeErrs split by "\n" gives each as separate line, each already "pos: msg". Good.
