	// no load errors, proceed to checking
	cwd, _ := os.Getwd()
	var reports []report
	seenFiles := map[string]bool{}
	// For checking, need to consider all files from all packages (deduplicated), but need correct info for each file (which package's info to use? Use first package that contains it in checkOrder? Or in pkgs order? To avoid duplicate, use first occurrence in pkgs order? Let's use pkgs order (go list order) for determinism? Or checkOrder? For single package with test variant, foo.go appears in both normal and test variant. Which info to use? Both should give same unchecked results for foo.go? Possibly same. Good. We'll use first occurrence in pkgs order (as returned).
	// Build map abs -> (info, fset, src, pkg)
